<%
const blurbs = {
  student: 'Part-time and student-friendly work that fits around your studies.',
  intern_coop: 'Internships and co-op placements that turn what you\'re learning into real experience.',
  graduate: 'A first full-time role after finishing your studies.',
  early_career: 'Entry-level and junior roles to build your track record.',
  skilled: 'Technical, trade and experienced roles for young professionals with real skills behind them.',
};
%>
<section class="about-section" id="who-we-serve" aria-labelledby="serve-h">
  <h2 id="serve-h">Explore your path: five stages, one Job Bank</h2>
  <p class="prose">Youth Futures Canada serves young people — not one kind of job. A student, a graduate, and a skilled professional with several years of experience are all part of the same audience; they're just at different points in the same journey.</p>
  <ul class="grid grid--5 about-aud">
    <% C.CAREER_STAGES.forEach(([key, name]) => { %>
      <li class="card about-aud__card about-aud__card--<%= key %>">
        <h3><a href="/jobs?stage=<%= key %>"><%= name %></a></h3>
        <p><%= blurbs[key] %></p>
      </li>
    <% }) %>
  </ul>
  <div class="prose">
    <h3>Real postings for every stage in Canada</h3>
    <p>A student can search for <a href="/jobs?stage=student">part-time student jobs</a>, someone finishing school can browse <a href="/jobs?stage=intern_coop">internships and co-ops</a> or <a href="/jobs?stage=graduate">graduate roles</a>, and an early-career candidate can filter for <a href="/jobs?stage=early_career">entry-level and junior opportunities</a>. Young professionals who already have real experience — a trade, a technical skill, a few years in the field — can go straight to <a href="/jobs?stage=skilled">skilled career opportunities</a> in <a href="/jobs?category=healthcare">healthcare and nursing</a>, <a href="/jobs?category=it_software">IT and software</a>, <a href="/jobs?category=engineering">engineering</a>, <a href="/jobs?category=construction_trades">construction and skilled trades</a>, <a href="/jobs?category=transport_logistics">transportation and logistics</a> and <a href="/jobs?category=accounting_finance">accounting and finance</a>. Every posting can also be tagged for the communities it explicitly welcomes — including new immigrants, Indigenous peoples and refugees — so that signal is searchable too.</p>
    <h3>Every province and territory, every major city</h3>
    <p>Youth Futures Canada lists jobs in all 13 provinces and territories — from <a href="/jobs?province=ON">Ontario</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=BC">British Columbia</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=AB">Alberta</a> and <a href="/jobs?province=QC">Quebec</a> to <a href="/jobs?province=MB">Manitoba</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=SK">Saskatchewan</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=NS">Nova Scotia</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=NB">New Brunswick</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=NL">Newfoundland and Labrador</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=PE">Prince Edward Island</a>, <a href="/jobs?province=YT">Yukon</a>, the <a href="/jobs?province=NT">Northwest Territories</a> and <a href="/jobs?province=NU">Nunavut</a>. Popular city searches include
      <% cities.forEach(([city, prov], i) => { %><a href="/jobs?province=<%= prov %>&city=<%= encodeURIComponent(city) %>">jobs in <%= city %></a><%= i < cities.length - 2 ? ', ' : (i === cities.length - 2 ? ' and ' : '.') %><% }) %></p>
  </div>
</section>
